  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kairouan Solar Plant</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project promises strong development impact in Tunisia as it is expected to (i) expand solar capacity to generate more efficient and environmentally friendly sources of energy to meet the growing local demand; (ii) contribute towards improved affordability of power by lowering the cost of generation, which is currently heavily reliant on imported fuel; (iii) contribute to power market competitiveness by attracting private sector participation; and (iv) enhance the power sector resilience by diversifying the countrys power generation mix, which currently has a very low share of green generation infrastructure.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed investment seeks to support a 100MW solar photovoltaic (PV) project in Tunisia under a 20-year Power Purchase Agreement with the Soci&#xe9;t&#xe9; Tunisienne de l&apos;Electricit&#xe9; et du Gaz (Tunisian Company of Electricity and Gas  STEG) (the Project)</narrative>
  </description>
